msgid "Enable"
msgstr ""

msgid "Starts the agent, enables it at boot, and opens TCP 8090 plus UDP 29820/29821 on the WAN zone, so an AC on the upstream or LAN side can discover and manage this access point during initial setup. On by default."
msgstr ""

msgid "Controller address"
msgstr ""

msgid "host:port of the controller. Leave empty to find the controller by UDP broadcast on the local segment; once it answers, the discovered address is filled in here and can be saved to pin it. A controller on the other side of a router must be entered explicitly, because broadcast never crosses layer 3."
msgstr ""

msgid "Shared secret"
msgstr ""

msgid "Must match AC_SHARED_SECRET on the controller. Leave empty when the controller does not check one."
msgstr ""

msgid "Heartbeat interval"
msgstr ""

msgid "Seconds between two polls. The default is 20."
msgstr ""

msgid "Peer coordination port"
msgstr ""

msgid "UDP port used to exchange 802.11k data between access points directly. 0 disables it."
msgstr ""

msgid "Peer announcement interval"
msgstr ""

msgid "How often this access point announces its BSS and client state to its peers, for example 30s."
msgstr ""

msgid "Peer coordination network"
msgstr ""

msgid "Logical OpenWrt network, for example lan, that carries AP-to-AP traffic. The agent resolves its l3_device and joins IPv6 link-local multicast on it; when IPv6 is unavailable it falls back to IPv4 broadcast."
msgstr ""

msgid "Peer shared secret"
msgstr ""

msgid "Shared by every access point and used to authenticate peer messages with HMAC-SHA256. Leave empty only on a trusted management segment; never reuse AC_SHARED_SECRET."
msgstr ""

msgid "Local roam suggestion"
msgstr ""

msgid "Let the agent itself send one 802.11v transition suggestion (BTM) when a client is very weak and a peer serves the same SSID. This is built into the agent, needs no steering daemon, and is on by default so roaming keeps working across any number of access points after the controller is lost. It stays silent whenever usteer or dawn is enabled; nrsyncd only distributes 11k neighbour lists and does not compete."
msgstr ""

